7-5095-9f12-acc78818a070" :question/math-academy-id "q-48843" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(1)=8,\\,{f}^{′}(1)=6,\\,g(1)=4,\\,{g}^{′}(1)=4\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=1} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(1)g(1)-f(1){g}^{′}(1)}{{g}^{2}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 4}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48843/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48843"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "907cd3df-81fe-5f32-82a1-04adc2978540" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "6e7e53cc-349f-5995-9aa7-cba29e855d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c8ccfb64-af42-5a0e-8d2c-b67030bad6ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer/id #uuid "d6ba6b3e-671f-5020-bbe2-995377926322" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "89140d3b-6096-5b43-942b-8c763d76294f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74eac84e-7d80-54a7-9ac7-d2f58632c75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48965/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-48965/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-48965/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-48965/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-48965/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" "q-48965/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48965" :question/id #uuid "18e1de8e-0324-5cfc-8ed1-bb965f60a808" :question/math-academy-id "q-48965" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(2)=-1,\\,{f}^{′}(2)=-2,\\,g(2)=-5,\\,{g}^{′}(2)=1\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{5f(x)+4}{g(x)+6},$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5f(x)+4$ and $v=g(x)+6.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(g(x)+6)\\cdot 5{f}^{′}(x)-(5f(x)+4)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x)+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{f}^{′}(x)(g(x)+6)-{g}^{′}(x)(5f(x)+4)}{(g(x)+6)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{5{f}^{′}(2)(g(2)+6)-{g}^{′}(2)(5f(2)+4)}{(g(2)+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5+6)-1\\cdot (5\\cdot (-1)+4)}{(-5+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot 1-(-1)}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-48965/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48965"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "df8dd3ba-115f-51c1-97ce-ad9f1a812238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "da73b34b-f20e-593e-94ea-81cf8410b666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b6dab45b-f6fd-55ec-89be-0f431180a5b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4c1bffdf-d21f-5cd8-a1ce-6bd2091d293d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1cfd21b5-68dc-558a-9523-667aa9fae254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "789dd413-fd19-5c2e-8d48-7c7725fcc86d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105493/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-105493/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-105493/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-105493/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-105493/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-105493/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105493" :question/id #uuid "c14bafb6-deba-59e6-83ba-5f1bd4461fa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-105493" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{3f(x)-1}{2g(x)+2},$ determine the value of ${h}^{′}(0).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3f(x)-1$ and $v=2g(x)+2.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2g(x)+2)\\cdot 3{f}^{′}(x)-(3f(x)-1)\\cdot 2{g}^{′}(x)}{(2g(x)+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{f}^{′}(x)(2g(x)+2)-2{g}^{′}(x)(3f(x)-1)}{(2g(x)+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{3{f}^{′}(0)(2g(0)+2)-2{g}^{′}(0)(3f(0)-1)}{(2g(0)+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0\\cdot (2\\cdot 1+2)-2\\cdot 2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3-1)}{(2\\cdot 1+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\cdot 8}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-105493/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105493"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341011/field-1/35748e359657fc688f8e279fcf2b56083d507afe79973cc88b169b63c7dcb719" :answer/id #uuid "79b19c4f-afcd-59f5-a05b-3b82e0363163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341011/field-1/7ca406ed6690410e3c85c046a8fc266540a56cf4545cf1cbb6354f4fdf108590" :answer/id #uuid "9a5a97e8-748e-5263-a931-6e1ae92cb731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341011/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c11a31b7-d8c5-5e46-9711-363f7936fd1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341011/field-1/35748e359657fc688f8e279fcf2b56083d507afe79973cc88b169b63c7dcb719" :answer-field/choices ["q-341011/field-1/35748e359657fc688f8e279fcf2b56083d507afe79973cc88b169b63c7dcb719" "q-341011/field-1/7ca406ed6690410e3c85c046a8fc266540a56cf4545cf1cbb6354f4fdf108590"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341011" :question/id #uuid "57f7ba5d-d0b2-5f0a-bf27-9c38b7d5be75" :question/math-academy-id "q-341011" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $4$ | $-1$ | $2$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(4)-(\\frac{1}{2})(2)}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-1}{16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341011/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341011"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341028/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8ee2f22c-0ceb-5f3b-8f8e-ebb97c7f902c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341028/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a537318f-83e9-5874-add3-56b0f3be2afe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341028/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-341028/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341028" :question/id #uuid "6d72eb11-db3f-5e0d-9fd0-7dd743dc99d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-341028" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=0$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=0.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0} & =3{q}^{′}(0)+4{r}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =3(2)+4(-1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341028/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93eb24a9-f358-50cf-b447-c394864843f9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341028"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
